---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Mirrors the in-app Terms of Service (SettingsView.swift). Keep the two in sync.
const contactEmail = 'support@pumpdeck.app';
const lastUpdated = 'May 6, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — PumpDeck"
  description="The terms that govern your use of PumpDeck."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-600">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div
      class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-ink-soft [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-ink [&_a]:text-brand-600 [&_a]:underline"
    >
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <p>
          These terms govern your use of PumpDeck. They will be reviewed by
          counsel before final App Store submission.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>1. The service</h2>
        <p>
          PumpDeck is a fitness logging app. It tracks workouts you record, plans
          you build, and body measurements you enter. It is provided as-is,
          without warranty of fitness for a particular purpose.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>2. Subscriptions and billing</h2>
        <p>
          PumpDeck offers auto-renewing subscriptions, billed through your App
          Store account. We offer monthly and yearly plans; the current price,
          and any free trial, are shown in the app before you subscribe.
        </p>
        <p>
          Payment is charged to your App Store account when you confirm the
          purchase. Your subscription renews automatically at the end of each
          billing period unless you turn off auto-renew at least 24 hours before
          the period ends. You can view, manage, or cancel your subscription
          anytime in your App Store account settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a free trial is offered, any unused portion is forfeited when you
          start a paid subscription. Refunds are handled by Apple under the App
          Store's standard policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>3. Not medical advice</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing in the app is medical, nutritional, or professional fitness
          advice. Lifting and training carry inherent risks. Consult a qualified
          professional before starting or changing any exercise program. You are
          solely responsible for the lifts you choose to perform and for the way
          you perform them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>4. Your account</h2>
        <p>
          You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account
          credentials. You must be at least 13 years old to create an account.
        </p>
        <p>
          You agree not to use the app to upload unlawful content, attempt to
          access other users' data, or interfere with the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>5. Content you create</h2>
        <p>
          You retain ownership of every workout, plan, photo, and note you
          create. You grant us a limited license to store and serve that content
          back to you on the devices where you sign in. We do not republish or
          resell your content.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>6. Termination</h2>
        <p>
          You can delete your account at any time from Settings. We may suspend
          or terminate accounts that violate these terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>7. Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, PumpDeck is not liable for
          indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of
          the app, including any injury sustained while training.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>8. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms; material changes will be surfaced in-app on
          next launch.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>9. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
